Hook: pick hook_type from {{ allowed_hooks | join(", ") }}.
{%- set formulas = {
  "why_question": "\"Why does/doesn't {machine} {surprising behavior}?\"",
  "hidden_inside": "\"You've seen this a thousand times, but never inside it.\"",
  "surprising_number": "\"{Big or small number} + {object}\"",
  "myth_bust": "\"Most people think {X}. Actually {Y}.\"",
  "what_if": "\"What happens if {part} fails or stops?\"",
  "reveal": "\"Inside this {object} is a {surprising thing}.\"",
} %}
{% for name in allowed_hooks %}- {{ name }}: {{ formulas[name] }}
{% endfor %}
Visual beats: Studio (object on a dark pedestal), Cutaway (casing opens to show the inside),
Flow (glowing energy moves through the parts), In situ (the part installed where it is used).
Pick beat_order from:
{%- set orders = {
  "classic": "studio, cutaway, flow, in_situ",
  "context_first": "in_situ, studio, cutaway, flow",
  "action_first": "flow, cutaway, studio, in_situ",
  "cold_open": "cutaway, flow, in_situ, studio",
} %}
{% for name in allowed_beats %}- {{ name }}: {{ orders[name] }}
{% endfor %}
Narration fields, each with its own word budget (count the words of each part before answering):
- hook: the first sentence, about {{ part_words.hook }} words.
- body: everything between hook and Engineer's Note, about {{ part_words.body }} words in short, plain sentences.
- engineer_note_draft: one sentence of genuine insight in the narrator's normal voice, for example
  "Here's the surprising part: ..." or "What most people miss is ...", about {{ part_words.note }} words. Never "As an engineer", never "I" or "me",
  and no claims of expertise. It is a draft the channel owner will edit, so make it a genuine, checkable
  observation, never a made-up personal story.
- loop_line: the last sentence. It must be a complete sentence that ends with a period, question mark or
  exclamation mark (never "..." or a dangling "because"), and it should lead naturally back to the hook when the video loops.
  About {{ part_words.loop }} words.
- Together that is about {{ target_words }} words. The total must stay between {{ min_words }} and {{ max_words }} words:
  going over is the most common mistake, so when in doubt, write less.

Shot list ("shots"), numbered from 1, covering the whole narration: shot durations must add up to at least the
narration's length, about {{ target_total_s }} seconds for {{ target_words }} words. Add stills or diagrams to fill time.
Do the sum before answering (a total that is too short is the most common mistake): for example {{ shot_seconds.clips }} flow_clips
x 8 s = {{ shot_seconds.clip_s }} s, so the diagrams and stills (3-6 s each) must add the other {{ shot_seconds.rest_s }} s.
Add up every duration_s: about {{ target_total_s }} s, never under {{ shot_seconds.min_total_s }} s; more words need more seconds.
- kind "flow_clip": an 8-second AI video clip, at most 8 seconds. Use {{ min_clips }} to {{ max_clips }} of them.
  Every flow_clip needs its beat's fields: studio -> hero_feature; cutaway -> internals and focus_part;
  flow -> energy (electric, heat or fluid), path and process; in_situ -> context.
- kind "still": an AI still image that will be slowly animated.
- kind "diagram": a label card drawn by code over the picture: "labels" holds 1-4 part names of at most 4 words each
  (e.g. ["Rotor", "Stator Coils", "Diode Bridge"]), and "energy" picks the colour of their dots. At least {{ min_diagrams }} diagrams.
  Every other shot has "labels": [].
- Every one of the four beats appears, and the first appearance of each beat follows the chosen beat_order.

Sources ("sources"): exactly 3 different real web pages that support the main facts, each with url, title, publisher and the claim it supports.
Every URL is checked automatically, so only cite pages you are sure exist. Prefer stable pages: Wikipedia articles,
university or standards-body pages, and long-standing technical references. Never guess a URL path.
